WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.190
The main lesson of this course is that people learn through active construction, not passive exposure.

2
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:15.476
They connect new information to prior knowledge, refine mental models, focus attention, manage cognitive load, practice retrieval, receive feedback, and apply skills in context.

3
00:00:15.476 --> 00:00:17.411
Each piece supports the others.

4
00:00:17.411 --> 00:00:22.440
Clear explanations matter, but explanations alone are rarely enough to create durable performance.

5
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.149
Strong learning design is practical and structured.

6
00:00:25.149 --> 00:00:33.661
It starts with the capability people need, then builds a path toward that capability through examples, sequencing, practice, feedback, review, and transfer.

7
00:00:33.661 --> 00:00:37.143
It respects the limits of attention and working memory.

8
00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:39.464
It uses relevance to support effort.

9
00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:43.333
It creates confidence through achievable challenge rather than empty reassurance.

10
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:46.041
It treats mistakes as data for improvement.

11
00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:49.910
The goal is not to make learners consume more content.

12
00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:56.101
The goal is to help them build understanding they can retrieve and skill they can use.

13
00:00:56.101 --> 00:01:06.934
When a learning experience is aligned with real performance, learners are more likely to remember what matters, recognize when to use it, and adapt it when conditions change.

14
00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:14.285
That is the difference between a course that was completed and learning that actually travels back to the work.

15
00:01:14.285 --> 00:01:19.315
As a practical takeaway, look at any learning experience and ask four questions.

16
00:01:19.315 --> 00:01:22.023
What will the learner need to do?

17
00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:26.279
What prior knowledge or misconception will shape how they understand it?

18
00:01:26.279 --> 00:01:29.375
Where will they practice and receive useful feedback?

19
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:34.404
How will the design help them use the skill later, outside the lesson?

20
00:01:34.404 --> 00:01:39.047
Those questions keep the work grounded in capability rather than content volume.
